The full set grants the following effects while equipped:
<tabber>
|-|With Headgear=
* +{{getSetInfo|Shroomite armor|defense|note=n}} [[defense]]
* +13% [[ranged damage]]
* ×1.12<ref name="multiplicative-increase"/> damage of [[bows]], [[repeaters]], [[arrows]], and [[Stake]]s
|-|With Mask=
* +{{getSetInfo|Shroomite armor|defense|note=n}} [[defense]]
* +13% [[ranged damage]]
* ×1.12<ref name="multiplicative-increase"/> damage of [[guns]], [[bullets]], and [[Candy Corn]]
|-|With Helmet=
* +{{getSetInfo|Shroomite armor|defense|note=n}} [[defense]]
* +13% [[ranged damage]]
* ×1.12<ref name="multiplicative-increase"/> damage of specialist ranged weapons (non-consumable ranged weapons that are not bows or guns) and their ammunition
</tabber>
* +25% ranged [[critical strike chance]]
* +20% [[ammo conservation]]
* +12% [[movement speed]]
* The player leaves dark blue afterimages when moving
* Standing still and not using any items causes the player to quickly enter [[stealth]], which causes them to turn almost invisible and prevents [[Fighter AI]] and [[Flying AI]] enemies from firing [[projectiles]] at the player while they are not using an item. Stealth is engaged gradually over the course of {{duration|ceil(1/0.015) ticks}}<!-- the player's stealth attribute is reduced by 0.015 every tick, going from 1 to 0 -->, during which the player gains several stat boosts that linearly increase to the following values:{{source code ref|v=1.4.4.9|method=Terraria.Player.Update / Terraria.Player.GetWeaponKnockback}}
** +60% ranged damage
** +10% ranged critical strike chance
** −750 [[aggro]]
** +50% ranged [[knockback]]

Stealth mode is deactivated upon riding a [[Mounts|mount]]{{source code ref|v=1.4.4.9|method=Terraria.Player.Update}} or taking damage{{source code ref|v=1.4.4.9|method=Terraria.Player.Hurt}}. Stealth mode will also fade once the player starts moving (''see [[#Notes|Notes]] for details'').

